      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="617493988">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="2500583">Count Smiley</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP321 Provost

We came into town from the south side and I was completely distracted by the impressive looking museum and the grounds around it.  Mr. C got my attention back to cap hunting and we were quickly at ground zero.   This cap has seen its share of battering of the years.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="615895669">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="228846">Mr. CanoeHead</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP321 Provost

The short grass and prominent ground post made this a quick find but then deciphering the numbers became the challenge.   This cap appears to have been hit by every farm implement, shovel and backhoe in Provost.   Main street Provost was torn up for some kind of road repair.    TFTCap&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="551704039">
          <groundspeak:date>2015-10-22T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="854786">antoncache</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP321 - Provost, AB

  N53 20.996   W110 16.119&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out caching with Hugh of CachingCarolandHugh and was in Provost, AB when Hugh tells me we just drove by a Brass Cap. We went back and made find easily enough. Hugh posted the pictures for the site. Thanks for the cap. TFTC!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="551693415">
          <groundspeak:date>2015-10-22T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3355355">CachingCarolandHugh</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt; BCP321 - Provost&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;N 52 20.996  W 110 16.119&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Found this cap in Provost today while out on a caching road trip with &quot;antoncahe&quot;.  It made for a long day, from Leduc to almost the Sask. border and back but it was a worth while and fun trip. And we get to claim this Brass Cap to boot. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;b&gt;TFTBCP - &quot; outforthehunt &quot; !!  &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_approve.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;...CachingCarolandHugh &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_tongue.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
